Implement user story AMSD-1820: [Mozio] - The Promo code amount is NOT displayed as expected for Return trip tickets in the Mozio email confirmation

## Story Description
[Mozio] - The Promo code amount is NOT displayed as expected for Return trip tickets in the Mozio email confirmation

## Acceptance Criteria
- The system displays the promo code discount amount in the Mozio email confirmation for the return trip portion when a return ticket is purchased with a promo code applied.
- The system displays the promo code discount amount for both the outbound and return trip portions in the Mozio email confirmation when a return ticket with a promo code is purchased.
- The system calculates the promo code discount amount for the return trip independently and shows a non-zero value when the promo code applies to the return portion.
- The system renders the promo code discount line item for each trip segment (outbound and return) separately in the email confirmation, so the customer can verify the discount for each leg.
- When a one-way ticket is purchased with a promo code, the system continues to display the promo code discount amount correctly in the Mozio email confirmation, confirming no regression for single-trip bookings.
- When the promo code discount amount is zero or not applicable to the return trip, the system omits the promo code discount line for the return trip and does not show an incorrect value or a missing placeholder token.
- The system includes the promo code identifier and the discounted total for both outbound and return trips in the email confirmation so the customer can reconcile the final charged amount per segment.
- Given a return ticket with a promo code applied, the email confirmation renders the correct discount amount for each trip segment, regardless of how the discount metadata is structured in the underlying order data.
- The promo code discount amount displayed in the email confirmation for each trip segment uses the correct currency symbol and decimal formatting consistent with the rest of the email.
- When a promo code discount equals or exceeds the cost of a trip segment, the email confirmation displays the full segment price as the discount amount and shows a zero or negative-adjusted total for that segment without rendering errors.
- When a promo code applies only to the outbound segment and not the return segment of a return ticket, the email confirmation shows the discount for the outbound segment and omits the discount line for the return segment.
- When a promo code applies only to the return segment and not the outbound segment of a return ticket, the email confirmation shows the discount for the return segment and omits the discount line for the outbound segment.
- When discount metadata is missing or malformed for one trip segment of a return ticket with a promo code, the email confirmation still renders correctly for the other segment and does not display a raw placeholder, undefined value, or error in the discount area.





